  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 110 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThe forecast starts out with northwest flow over the Central High \nPlains and Great Plains. Expect a beautiful afternoon across the \nregion with highs reaching the mid-70s. Breezy conditions are \nexpected through the afternoon, particularly for the northern and \neastern portions of the CWA. \n\nWarmer air gets ushered into the region as a warm front crosses the \nDakotas on Tuesday. Summer-like temperatures return briefly, \nreaching the upper 70s across portions of western Iowa and the low \nto mid-80s for much of eastern Nebraska. \n\nDry conditions continue through at least Wednesday morning, allowing \nareas to continue to recover from last week's flooding. A cold front \nis expected to drop into the region during the day, bringing some \nslightly cooler temperatures to the region (70s). A few models have \nstarted showing a low-end potential for some rain Wednesday \nnight/early Thursday morning. Have opted to hold off on adding a \nmention for now, but will continue to need to monitor any changes \nfor the need for a possible increase in PoPs. Thursday also brings a \nchance (20-30%) of a few showers/isolated thunderstorms.\n\nA ridge shifts east across Nebraska on Friday and Saturday. Warmer \ntemperatures are expected, particularly Saturday with highs \nreturning to the upper 70s to low 80s for many.",
